# Brenton's Septuagint → the Clementine Vulgate (content/bible/vulgate), read by
# lxx.py over SIL's draft (lxx.vrs → org → vul.vrs). Only where the draft is
# wrong or silent. `slug c:v[-v] = c:v[-v]` maps a range verse for verse (or
# onto one verse); `= -` marks a Greek verse with no counterpart. Each block was
# settled by reading the Greek beside the Latin; the last section (Tobias,
# Judith, Ecclesiasticus, which SIL leaves unmapped and where the Vulgate
# follows another text) was aligned verse by verse through Brenton's English
# and the Douay and spot-checked: it is approximate where Jerome paraphrases.

